<% title "Terms of Service" %>

<h1 class="heading">Terms of Service</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated 2 August 2026.</p>

<%= render "application/callout", type: "warning", title: "These are beta terms" do %>
  <p class="m0">
    Fuime is in a pre-launch beta. Payments and cards run against Stripe's test
    mode, which means <strong>no real money moves through Fuime</strong>. These
    terms describe that beta. Before Fuime handles real money they will be
    replaced by terms reviewed by a lawyer, and you will be asked to accept the
    new ones.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>1. Who you are agreeing with</h2>
<p>
  Fuime is a product of
  <strong><%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %></strong>. These
  terms are an agreement between you and that company. Where this page says
  &ldquo;Fuime&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, or &ldquo;us&rdquo;, it means
  <%= Rails.configuration.constants.legal_entity_name %>.
</p>
<p>
  If the account belongs to someone under 18, the person agreeing to these terms
  is their parent or legal guardian, under the
  <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path %>.
</p>

<h2>2. What Fuime is</h2>
<p>
  Fuime is software for keeping the books of a small business run by someone
  aged 13 to 17, with a parent or legal guardian on the account. It records
  income and expenses, stores receipts, and produces summaries that help at tax
  time.
</p>

<h2>3. What Fuime is not</h2>
<p>This matters more than anything else on this page.</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Fuime is not a bank</strong> and does not hold deposits. It is not
    a credit union, and money recorded in Fuime is not insured by the FDIC or
    anyone else.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Fuime is not a fiscal sponsor.</strong> It does not take legal
    ownership of your business or its money.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Fuime does not give tax, legal, or financial advice.</strong> The
    tax figures Fuime shows are estimates generated from the records you enter.
    They are not a tax return, not a determination of what you owe, and not a
    substitute for a professional. Check them with an accountant before relying
    on them.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>During the beta, Fuime does not move real money.</strong> Anything
    that looks like a payment or a card is running in test mode.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Who may use Fuime</h2>
<ul>
  <li>You must be at least 13 years old. There are no exceptions.</li>
  <li>
    If you are under 18, you must have an active guardian on your account
    before you can create or run a business. A parent or legal guardian accepts
    the <%= link_to "Guardian Agreement", guardian_agreement_path %> and takes
    legal responsibility for your use of Fuime.
  </li>
  <li>
    If you are 18 or over, you may use Fuime on your own behalf.
  </li>
  <li>
    You must give us accurate information, including a truthful answer when we ask
    whether you are old enough to use Fuime. Accounts built on false information
    can be closed.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Your account</h2>
<p>
  Keep your sign-in details to yourself. You are responsible for what happens
  under your account. Tell us at <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> if you
  think someone else has access to it. We recommend turning on two-factor
  authentication.
</p>

<h2>6. Your business and your records</h2>
<p>
  Your business is yours. Fuime does not own it, does not take a stake in it,
  and does not control it. The records you put into Fuime are yours too, and
  you can ask for a copy at any time.
</p>
<p>
  You are responsible for the accuracy of what you enter, and for meeting the
  legal obligations of running a business, including tax filings and any
  licences your local authority requires.
</p>

<h2>7. Fees</h2>
<p>
  When Fuime processes a payment for a business, it keeps
  <%= Fuime::PaymentLinkService::FUIME_PLATFORM_FEE_PERCENT %>% of that payment
  as a platform fee, shown as a separate line on the ledger. If we change the
  fee, we will tell you before it applies to you.
</p>

<%# Fuime: the sale-and-refunds section, added 2026-08-19.

    This is the load-bearing document for FEATURE_MERCHANT_OF_RECORD. Customer
    money landing in Fuime's own Stripe balance is Fuime's OWN revenue — and
    therefore lawful without a money-transmitter licence — only if Fuime is really
    the seller. That is established by terms that say so and by Fuime actually
    carrying the refund and chargeback obligation, not by anything in the code.
    See docs/fuime/MOR_RISK_ACCEPTANCE.md §2 Q1.

    Written to be true of the system as built: Fuime takes the payment, Fuime is
    named on the card statement ("Fuime* ..."), Fuime issues the refund, and the
    operator is paid afterwards as a vendor.

    ⚠️ THE 14-DAY WINDOW IS A DEFAULT, NOT A DECISION. It was chosen so the
