<h2>8. Buying through Fuime</h2>
<p>
  This section is for <strong>customers</strong> — anyone paying for a service
  they found through Fuime.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Fuime LLC is the seller.</strong> When you pay through Fuime, your
  contract for that purchase is with Fuime LLC, not with the young person or the
  business fulfilling it. Fuime takes your payment, Fuime appears on your card
  statement, Fuime sends your receipt, and Fuime is responsible to you for the
  purchase. The business you chose performs the work; we pay them afterwards as
  our vendor.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Refunds.</strong> If the service has not been performed yet, you can
  cancel and get a full refund. If something has gone wrong with a service that
  was performed, contact us within <strong>14 days</strong> of the purchase and we
  will look into it and put it right, which may mean a full or partial refund.
  Refunds are paid by Fuime and go back to the card you used.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>Disputes.</strong> Please contact us before disputing a charge with your
  bank — we can usually resolve it faster. Either way, the chargeback is ours to
  answer, not the young person's.
</p>
<p>
  <strong>How to reach us.</strong> Email
  <a href="mailto:support@fuime.com">support@fuime.com</a> with your receipt and
  what happened. A young founder is not the right person to handle a payment
  problem, and it is not their job to.
</p>

<h2>9. What you may not do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Break the law, or use Fuime to help someone else break the law.</li>
  <li>
    Use Fuime for anything on
    <%= link_to "Stripe's restricted businesses list", "https://stripe.com/legal/restricted-businesses", target: "_blank" %>.
  </li>
  <li>Misrepresent who you are, how old you are, or who your guardian is.</li>
  <li>
    Invite someone who is not your parent or legal guardian to act as your
    guardian.
  </li>
  <li>
    Attack, overload, or try to break into Fuime. If you want to report a
    vulnerability, see our <%= link_to "security page", security_path %> — we
    would genuinely like to hear from you.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>10. A guardian can end this at any time</h2>
<p>
  A parent or guardian may withdraw consent whenever they choose. When they do,
  the teen can no longer operate a business on Fuime. Records are kept
  according to our <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %>.
</p>

<h2>11. We can end it too</h2>
<p>
  We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, or where we
  believe someone is at risk. Where we can, we will tell you why and give you a
  chance to get your records out first.
</p>

<h2>12. No warranty</h2>
<p>
  Fuime is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo;. This is beta software. It may have
  bugs, it may be unavailable, and it may get something wrong. We do not
  promise it is error-free or that it will always be running.
</p>

<h2>13. Limit of liability</h2>
<p>
  To the extent the law allows, Fuime is not liable for indirect or
  consequential losses, or for lost profits. Nothing here limits liability that
  cannot legally be limited.
</p>

<h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>
  We will update the date at the top when these change. For a material change
